--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Privacy / telemetry
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TDPdf does not phone home by default. Released binaries ship with no
telemetry endpoint embedded. The Application Insights SDK is initialized
at startup but operates as a no-op unless an administrator has explicitly
provisioned a connection-string file at:

    %ProgramData%\TDPdf\telemetry.dat

The file is DPAPI-encrypted (LocalMachine scope) with a fixed entropy
parameter and ACL'd so that only SYSTEM and BuiltinAdministrators can
modify it. The file is created by running, from an elevated context:

    type conn.txt | TDPdf.exe /set-telemetry

It can be removed at any time with:

    TDPdf.exe /clear-telemetry

When provisioned, TDPdf emits anonymous usage events (App.Startup,
Tool.Selected, File.Open/New/Save/SaveFlattened/Merge/Split/Print,
Install.Start/Success, Install.Crash, Crash) to the configured Azure
Application Insights resource. File paths, file names, document content,
user names, and persistent device identifiers are not emitted. Stack
traces are scrubbed of paths before transmission. Each session is
anonymous; no User.Id or Device.Id is set. See
docs/intune-distribution.md for provisioning and key-rotation details.

